\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every integer $n>=3$ and every f in $H^(n/(2(n+1)))(R^n)$, does its Schrodinger evolution, interpreted as the limit of Gaussian frequency regularizations, admit a representative converging to f almost everywhere as time decreases to zero?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every integer $n>=3$ and every f in $H^(n/(2(n+1)))(R^n)$, does its Schrodinger evolution, interpreted as the limit of Gaussian frequency regularizations, admit a representative converging to f almost everywhere as time decreases to zero?

